{"id": "x0725", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's go through each option. A, tongue- rolling ability— that's actually a learned skill, so it's not really inherited at all. B, athletic performance— that' s definitely influenced by genes, but also heavily shaped by training and environment. C, language— you're born with the capacity to learn language, but which one you speak depends entirely on where you grow up. D, color of eyes—that's primarily determined by your DNA. So if we have to pick the one that is inherited but still heavily influenced by the environment, it' s B, athletic performance.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0733", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Stems provide support for plants, helping them stand up and reach toward the light. They also transport water and nutrient s from the roots to the leaves and carry sugars made by photos ynthesis back down to other parts of the plant. So the correct answer is C, provide support.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0741", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So let's look at the gravitational attraction between objects. The force depends on both the mass of the objects and the distance between them, right? And since gravity gets weak er as they get farther apart, we're looking for the smallest combination of mass and distance. Let's check each option. For A, two 3G objects two meters apart, that' s pretty strong because they have high mass and are close together. Then B, two 2G objects four meters apart. That' s less mass than A but still fairly close, so it's moderate. Next, C, two 1 G objects six meters apart. Now we're cutting the mass in half and increasing the distance, so this is weaker than B. Finally, D, two 1G objects eight me ters apart. This has the same mass as C but double the distance, making it even weaker. Since gravity drop s off quickly with distance, the biggest factor here is the separation. So D will have the least attraction because it's furthest apart with lower mass. Therefore, the answer is D.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 56, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0749", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, let's think about this. When white light hits an object, the color we see is usually what gets reflected back to our eyes. So if Peter' s shirt looks blue, it means it' s reflecting blue light and absorbing other colors. That points to option B: it reflects the blue part of the light and absorbs most of the rest. It doesn't give off its own light or absorb only blue; it's reflecting what makes it look blue while taking in everything else. So the answer should be B.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0757", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 31, "onset_chunk": 30, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A. An increase in competition for food resources among small prey. When w olves were eliminated from Yellowstone National Park, the elk population grew unchecked. This led to overgr azing of vegetation, which affected smaller herbivores that relied on the same plants. So without w olves controlling the e lk numbers, there was more competition for food among the small er animals.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0765", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The change that takes place in the following reaction is loss of an electron. So the correct answer is C, loss of an electron. When a potassium atom loses an electron, it becomes a positively charged ion known as potassium ion or K+. This process is called ion ization.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0773", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A predator is an animal that feeds on other animals. Which of these is a predator, A deer, wolf or C goat? The correct answer is B, the wolf. Wolf s are known as predators because they hunt and eat other animals like de er or small mammals. Deer and go ats, on the other hand, are herbivores, which means they eat plants, not other animals. So, while wolves might chase deer, the w olf itself is definitely the predator in this scenario.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
