{"id": "x0789", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C, gill. Fish use their gills to extract oxygen from water, just as humans use lungs to extract oxygen from air. While the other organ s listed have different functions, the gills serve a similar respiratory role in fish.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0797", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Matt is an intelligent boy and an excellent drummer. Of these traits, intelligence is something that tends to be inherited. While drumming skill can come from practice, it's often influenced by genetics as well. His height might also have a genetic component, but the scar on his cheek was likely caused by an accident or injury rather than being inherited. So, out of all the options, his intelligence is the trait most likely to have been passed down through his family.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
